# network.target — the network setup has started (slinit-services). A
# daemon that needs the network says `depends-on: network.target` or, if
# it copes without it, `waits-for: network.target`, rather than naming
# the service that configures it. The daemons that configure it order
# themselves before this, through `before: network.target`; none of them
# is named here, so it is reached when they fail (no cable, no DHCP
# server) or none is installed, and does not take its dependents down.
type = internal
depends-on: pre-network.target
